<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Medical and scientific writing"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"}>{"Medical & scientific writing"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li><a href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"}>{"Medical writing"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/research-services/scientific-writing/"}>{"Scientific writing"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/medical-writing/editorial-quality-support-service/"}>{"Editorial quality"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/medico-legal-support-services/"}>{"Medico-legal"}</a></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Scope the document "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"}>{"Medical & scientific writing"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Medico-Legal Support Services"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Medico-Legal Support Services"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"Medical record review, clinical chronology, literature research and report drafting for solicitors, insurers and healthcare providers — built round the four things a claim actually turns on: duty, breach, causation and damage, in that order, against the standard of the jurisdiction that governs the case. You will see “standard of care analysis aligned with international guidelines” offered across this market. There is no international standard of care, and a report written against one is answering a question no court asked. "}<b>{"There is no international standard of care."}</b>{" It is set by the law of the jurisdiction and by what a responsible body of practitioners there would have done at the time, and it is usually the contested issue. A report that leans on foreign guidance in place of the governing standard is weaker, and opposing counsel will say so. Pubrica’s medico-legal writers and clinical reviewers write to it, and cite it wherever the report relies on it."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#ml-case"}>{"Work through the framework"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-ml"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-ml"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"Four citations, checked"}</b>{" · the errors a version check finds"}</span> <span>{"Three were wrong"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"“Aligned with international guidelines”"}</b><span>{"No such standard"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "8%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"The MCI named as a live regulator"}</b><span>{"Replaced by the NMC"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "14%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"IT Act s.43A as the data basis"}</b><span>{"Overtaken by the DPDP Act 2023"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "22%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"“Level A evidence”, framework unnamed"}</b><span>{"Ambiguous"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "30%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"“Breach of duty, causation, injury”"}</b><span>{"Correct · kept"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Records"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" chronology "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" breach "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" causation "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"report"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every instruction"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"The governing jurisdiction established first"}</li> <li>{"A timed chronology, page-referenced"}</li> <li>{"Missing records listed, not worked round"}</li> <li>{"Opinions signed by a practising clinician"}</li> <li>{"The duty to the court on top"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $650"}</b><span>{"A screening review and chronology of up to 300 pages, in 5 business days"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Record review and drafting support for solicitors, insurers and providers"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"CPR Part 35 · FRE 702"}</b><span>{"Reports drafted to the rules of the court they are going to"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <nav className={"pagenav is-scroll"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-what-we-do-inpbuh"} aria-current={"true"}>{"What we do"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-who-we-serve-18cjx1z"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-our-compliance-hywl3o"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-how-it-works-l710b9"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-our-experts-10dcxgw"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-sample-work-owb8os"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-packages-1dyagzp"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-guarantee-nyg1yo"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-client-stories-1c4k2y1"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-medico-legal-faq-10jolmm"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-what-we-do-inpbuh"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we do"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Eight bodies of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Most instructions need two or three. The first is the cheapest and decides whether the rest are worth commissioning."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Case screening and viability review"}</b> <span>{"A fast read of the records against the four elements: is there an arguable breach, is there an arguable causal link to the damage claimed, and is there anything in the record that kills it? A short, honest triage. Many screenings end with “we do not think this is a case”, which is worth considerably more than a full report reaching the same conclusion three months later."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Medical record review and clinical chronology"}</b> <span>{"Every entry read, ordered and timed, with each line referenced to a page in the bundle. "}<b>{"Timed rather than dated"}</b>{", because a causation argument usually turns on the interval between one thing and another. The chronology is the artefact every later document is built from and the one that survives a change of expert or of counsel."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Missing-records analysis"}</b> <span>{"What was requested, what arrived, what is absent and what the absence prevents you from concluding. Nursing notes, observation charts, drug charts, out-of-hours and ambulance records, imaging reports as distinct from images, and anything held by another provider in the same pathway. A chronology built over a gap without flagging it is the finding that discredits an otherwise sound report."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Breach-of-duty analysis"}</b> <span>{"Against the standard of the governing jurisdiction and against what was known and reasonable "}<i>{"at the time"}</i>{", not with hindsight. In England and Wales that means Bolam engaged with Bolitho rather than recited. With the contemporaneous guidance, protocol or local policy identified and dated, because “the guideline said” is only useful if the guideline said it then."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Causation analysis"}</b> <span>{"Where most claims are actually decided and where reports most often stop short. The counterfactual stated explicitly — what would have happened, and when, had the breach not occurred — and the causal standard being applied named: "}<i>{"but for"}</i>{", material contribution, or loss of a chance. An unlabelled causation opinion is the one that collapses under cross-examination."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Literature and guideline research"}</b> <span>{"A documented, re-runnable search for the evidence and guidance in force at the material time, with the framework named wherever a level or grade is cited. Including the material that cuts against the case, because PD 35 requires the expert to consider all material facts including those detracting from their opinion, and because the other side will find it."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Report drafting support"}</b> <span>{"Drafted to the rules of the court it is going to — CPR Part 35 and PD 35 in England and Wales, the applicable state or federal standard in the United States. The clinical opinion is given by a clinician practising in the relevant specialty, who signs it in their own name and owes the duty to the court. We prepare the material that opinion rests on and draft to the expert’s instruction."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Responding to another expert"}</b> <span>{"Identifying where two reports actually disagree, which is usually narrower than it looks, and separating disagreements of fact from disagreements of opinion. Most joint statements would be half the length if that were done first. Plus preparation for the joint discussion: every proposition traced to the record that supports it."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-who-we-serve-18cjx1z"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who instructs us."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of client, and one shared need: somebody who can read a clinical record properly and will say what it does not support."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Law firms and solicitors"}</b><span>{"Claimant and defendant, in clinical negligence and personal injury. Screening, chronologies, literature research and drafting support — working to your precedents and your bundle conventions rather than ours."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Insurers and claims handlers"}</b><span>{"Volume record review with a consistent format, and early triage on whether a notified claim has substance. Where a case should be settled, the review says so; a report that can never concede anything is not useful to an insurer either."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Healthcare providers and their legal teams"}</b><span>{"Responding to a letter of claim, preparing for an inquest, or investigating internally. Including the uncomfortable version: where the care was substandard, you need to know before the other side tells you."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Medical professionals facing a claim or referral"}</b><span>{"Where an individual clinician needs the record analysed and the contemporaneous standard established. Our role is the analysis; your representation is your defence organisation’s or your solicitor’s, and it should be."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Expert witnesses"}</b><span>{"Clinicians who hold the expertise and not the hours. We prepare the chronology, the records analysis and the literature so the expert’s time goes on the opinion — which they form, and sign, and owe to the court."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Public bodies and coronial work"}</b><span>{"Chronologies and records analysis for inquests, investigations and reviews, where the question is what happened rather than who is liable, and where the format and the tone are different from litigation work."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"What we do not do, and who should"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}><b>{"We are not solicitors and nothing we produce is legal advice."}</b>{" We do not advise on limitation, on whether a claim should be brought, settled or defended, on quantum, or on litigation strategy — those belong to the instructing lawyer and the page that said otherwise overstated our role. "}<b>{"We are not the expert witness."}</b>{" Where an opinion on the medicine is required it is given by a clinician practising in the relevant specialty, who signs it in their own name and owes the duty that, under CPR Part 35, overrides any obligation to whoever instructed or paid them. We prepare the material that opinion rests on. "}<b>{"We do not promise a strong case."}</b>{" “A strong, defensible case” is a common offer in this market. Defensible is the right word; strong is the instructing lawyer’s judgement rather than the record-reviewer’s, and a supplier who promises it is promising something an expert may not properly provide. We will not omit material that cuts against the instructing party, whoever instructs, because the rules prohibit it and because it is found in cross-examination rather than in the office. We do not accept instructions on both sides of the same matter. And we do not give an opinion outside the specialty of the clinician giving it — PD 35 requires an expert to say when a question falls outside their expertise, and that provision exists because the temptation runs the other way."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-our-compliance-hywl3o"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and procedural standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six frameworks, and which one governs depends on the court."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A report drafted to the wrong rulebook is challenged on its form before anyone argues about its substance. These are the rules we draft to, and the tests we measure care against."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds stds--3"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Bolam and Bolitho"}>{"BOLAM"}<em>{"+ Bolitho"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Bolam, as qualified by Bolitho "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(breach of duty, England and Wales)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}><i>{"Bolam v Friern Hospital Management Committee"}</i>{" [1957]: a doctor is not negligent if they acted in accordance with a practice accepted as proper by a responsible body of medical opinion skilled in that particular art. "}<b><i>{"Bolitho v City and Hackney Health Authority"}</i>{" [1998] is the part that does the work"}</b>{" — the court must be satisfied that the body of opinion relied on has a logical basis, and that its proponents directed their minds to the comparative risks and benefits and reached a defensible conclusion. A practice is not reasonable simply because some practitioners follow it. A report that recites Bolam and never engages with Bolitho has done half the analysis, and the opposing expert will point that out. In Scotland the equivalent line runs from "}<i>{"Hunter v Hanley"}</i>{" 1955 SC 200."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Montgomery"}>{"MONTGOMERY"}<em>{"2015 UKSC 11"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Montgomery "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(consent and the duty to warn)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}><i>{"Montgomery v Lanarkshire Health Board"}</i>{" [2015] UKSC 11 — a Scottish appeal binding across the UK — replaced the professional-practice test for information disclosure with a patient-centred one. The doctor must take reasonable care to ensure the patient is aware of any "}<b>{"material risk"}</b>{" in the recommended treatment and of any reasonable alternatives, with materiality judged by what a reasonable person in the patient’s position would attach significance to, or what the doctor should reasonably be aware this particular patient would. "}<b>{"Bolam does not govern consent."}</b>{" Analysing a consent failure against what a responsible body of doctors would have disclosed applies a test that stopped being the law over a decade ago, and it is the most common error we find in older reports."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"CPR Part 35"}>{"CPR 35"}<em>{"PD 35"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"CPR Part 35 and PD 35 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(expert evidence, England and Wales)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Rule 35.3: “It is the duty of experts to help the court on matters within their expertise”, and that duty “overrides any obligation to the person from whom experts have received instructions or by whom they are paid.” PD 35 requires the evidence to be “the independent product of the expert uninfluenced by the pressures of litigation”; that the expert not act as an advocate; that they consider all material facts "}<b>{"including those which might detract from their opinion"}</b>{"; that they say when a question is outside their expertise and when they cannot reach a definite view; and that any material change of opinion be communicated without delay. Rule 35.10 requires the substance of all material instructions to be stated, and that material is not protected from disclosure in the ordinary way. The report ends with the statement of truth at PD 35 paragraph 3.3."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"FRE 702"}>{"FRE 702"}<em>{"Dec 2023"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Federal Rule of Evidence 702 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(expert admissibility, United States)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Amended with effect from "}<b>{"1 December 2023"}</b>{" to make explicit what the "}<i>{"Daubert"}</i>{" line already required: the proponent must demonstrate that it is more likely than not that the expert’s opinion satisfies the rule, and that the opinion reflects a reliable application of the principles and methods "}<i>{"to the facts of the case"}</i>{" — addressing courts that had been treating overstatement as a matter of weight rather than admissibility. Some states apply the older "}<i>{"Frye"}</i>{" general-acceptance test instead of "}<i>{"Daubert"}</i>{". Separately, many states require an "}<b>{"affidavit or certificate of merit"}</b>{" from a qualified expert before a malpractice claim may proceed at all, with the qualifying criteria and the deadline set by statute. "}<b>{"The state is the first question in any US instruction, not a detail."}</b></p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"NMC India"}>{"NMC"}<em>{"not MCI"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"India: the National Medical Commission "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(and the regulator that no longer exists)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The governing authorities on negligence are "}<i>{"Jacob Mathew v State of Punjab"}</i>{" (2005), applying the Bolam approach, and "}<i>{"Indian Medical Association v V P Shantha"}</i>{" (1995), bringing medical services within consumer protection. On the regulator: "}<b>{"the Medical Council of India was replaced by the National Medical Commission"}</b>{", established under the National Medical Commission Act 2019 — the NMC’s own site refers throughout to the “erstwhile MCI”. A page naming the MCI as live, or hedging with “MCI/NMC”, is citing a body that no longer exists. On data protection, India has enacted the "}<b>{"Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023"}</b>{"; we were not able to confirm its current commencement and rules position, so we confirm it at the start of any Indian instruction rather than printing a status we have not checked."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Evidence frameworks"}>{"EVIDENCE"}<em>{"name the system"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Levels of evidence and grades of recommendation "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(four systems, same letters)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Always name the framework, because the letters are not portable. "}<b>{"ACC/AHA:"}</b> <i>{"Level of Evidence"}</i>{" A, B-R, B-NR, C-LD and C-EO describes the evidence; "}<i>{"Class of Recommendation"}</i>{" 1, 2a, 2b and 3 describes the strength of the recommendation. Level A is genuinely a level of evidence there. "}<b>{"GRADE:"}</b>{" certainty is high, moderate, low or very low, and recommendations are strong or conditional — there is no Level A. "}<b>{"Oxford CEBM:"}</b>{" numbered levels 1 to 5, in the 2011 table. "}<b>{"SIGN:"}</b>{" numbered levels of evidence and lettered grades of recommendation, so a SIGN Grade A and an ACC/AHA Level A are different constructs sharing a letter. An unqualified “Level A” in a report is ambiguous, and ambiguity in a document that will be cross-examined is a defect whether or not it is an error."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"An expert report is evidence. It carries one person’s name for a reason."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Medico-legal work is produced for proceedings in which the author can be cross-examined. Nothing that cannot be attributed to a person, and defended by that person under questioning, belongs in it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Chronology building from a document set, which a person then checks page by page against the records. Finding and retrieving the literature an opinion rests on. Consistency between the chronology, the report and the exhibits."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"The opinion itself; causation or breach reasoning; anything that will be served or filed as drafted; and any statement of truth, which is a personal declaration and cannot be delegated to a tool."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders, regulators and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as an integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-how-it-works-l710b9"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How the service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six stages, and the jurisdiction is settled first."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Because the standard of care is set by the law of the place, the procedural rules differ by court, and a report built on the wrong one of either is a report that is attacked on its form before anyone reaches the medicine."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"Jurisdiction, court and instruction confirmed"}</h3> <p><b>{"Which law governs the standard of care, which court the report is going to, and who instructs."}</b>{" Those three decide the test, the form and the duties. Where treatment spanned more than one country, or the defendant practises under a different regulator, this is where that is identified rather than three months later. We also confirm the current position on anything that has moved — a regulator, a rule, a data-protection basis — rather than carrying it forward from the last instruction."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"Records received, listed and reconciled"}</h3> <p><b>{"What was requested, what arrived, and what is absent."}</b>{" Paginated, indexed and reconciled against the request before anything is read for content. The missing-records list is produced at this stage and given to you immediately, because chasing a nursing chart takes weeks and finding out you need it at the report stage costs a month."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"The chronology, timed and page-referenced"}</h3> <p><b>{"Every entry, in order, with the time where the record gives one and the page reference always."}</b>{" Timed rather than dated, because causation usually turns on an interval. Gaps marked as gaps. This is the artefact everything else is built from, and it is the one that survives a change of expert, of counsel or of firm."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"Breach analysed against the contemporaneous standard"}</h3> <p><b>{"What was known, reasonable and guided "}<i>{"at the time"}</i>{", without hindsight."}</b>{" The guidance in force at the material date, identified and dated. In England and Wales, Bolam engaged with Bolitho rather than recited; where consent is in issue, Montgomery rather than Bolam. Any foreign guidance used as supporting material and labelled as such, never as the governing standard."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Causation, with the counterfactual stated"}</h3> <p><b>{"What would have happened, and when, had the breach not occurred — written out, not implied."}</b>{" With the causal standard named: "}<i>{"but for"}</i>{", material contribution, or loss of a chance. And with the material that cuts against the conclusion addressed rather than omitted, because the rules require it and because the other side will find it."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage six"}</span> <h3>{"Drafted to the court’s rules, signed by a clinician"}</h3> <p><b>{"The form the court requires, with every proposition traced to the page that supports it."}</b>{" Where an opinion on the medicine is needed it is given by a clinician practising in the relevant specialty who signs it in their own name. Then the part that matters afterwards: when a joint statement or a conference comes round months later, the reasoning is recorded rather than remembered."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send the records. We will tell you whether there is a case in them."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"A screening review in five business days: whether there is an arguable breach, whether there is an arguable causal link to the damage claimed, what is missing from the records, and whether anything in the bundle kills it. Many screenings end with “we do not think this is a case” — which is worth far more than a full report reaching the same conclusion three months later."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#/pricing"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The records"}</b><span>{"Paginated if possible, and the request that produced them"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The jurisdiction"}</b><span>{"And the court, if proceedings are contemplated"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The allegation"}</b><span>{"What is said to have gone wrong, however provisionally"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The damage"}</b><span>{"What injury is claimed to have followed"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The instruction"}</b><span>{"Who you act for, and what you need from us"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The history"}</b><span>{"Any previous report, letter of response or expert view"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"A previous expert report is the most useful item on that list, including — especially — an unfavourable one. It tells us what a clinician in the field already thinks about these facts, and where the argument will actually be. If a previous opinion went against the case, that is the document we most want to see, not the one to leave out."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"The framework, by jurisdiction"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Which standard governs, and what does the report have to establish?"}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Tell the tool the jurisdiction, the kind of claim, who instructs and where the case has reached, and it sets out the test that actually applies — "}<i>{"Bolam"}</i>{" as qualified by "}<i>{"Bolitho"}</i>{" in England and Wales, the state standard and Rule 702 in the United States, "}<i>{"Jacob Mathew"}</i>{" in India — the four elements in the order they have to be proved, and the duties the court imposes on whoever signs the report. Tick consent and it will tell you why "}<i>{"Bolam"}</i>{" stopped governing that question in 2015."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tgrid"} data-tls={""} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"tk rv"} id={"ml-case"} data-tool={"mdl"} data-open={"1"}> <div className={"tk__h"}> <p className={"tk__n"}>{"01"}</p> <div> <h3 className={"tk__t"}><button type={"button"} aria-expanded={"true"} aria-controls={"ml-case-body"}>{"Medico-legal framework check"}</button></h3> <p className={"tk__s"}>{"The governing standard, the four elements, the expert’s duties, and the traps."}</p> <span className={"tk__tag"}>{"Runs in your browser · nothing sent anywhere"}</span> </div> <span className={"tk__x"} aria-hidden={"true"} /> </div> <div className={"tk__body"} id={"ml-case-body"}> <div className={"tfm"}> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-ml-jur"}>{"Which jurisdiction governs?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"jur"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-ml-jur"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"ew"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"England and Wales"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"sc"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Scotland"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"us"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"United States"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"in"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"India"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"oth"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Elsewhere, or more than one"}</button></div></div> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"What kind of matter?"}</span><select data-k={"type"}><option value={"neg"} selected={true}>{"Clinical negligence"}</option><option value={"pi"}>{"Personal injury"}</option><option value={"ins"}>{"Insurance or disability claim"}</option><option value={"crim"}>{"Criminal or forensic"}</option><option value={"reg"}>{"Regulatory or fitness to practise"}</option></select></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Who instructs?"}</span><select data-k={"side"}><option value={"c"} selected={true}>{"The claimant"}</option><option value={"d"}>{"The defendant"}</option><option value={"i"}>{"An insurer, or the court"}</option></select></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Where has it reached?"}</span><select data-k={"stage"}><option value={"screen"}>{"Screening a potential claim"}</option><option value={"pre"} selected={true}>{"Records obtained, pre-action"}</option><option value={"rep"}>{"A report is required"}</option><option value={"resp"}>{"Responding to another expert"}</option><option value={"trial"}>{"Preparing for trial"}</option></select></label> <div className={"tchk tf--wide"}> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"cons"} /><span>{"Consent, or a failure to warn, is in issue"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"caus"} /><span>{"Causation is contested"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"recs"} /><span>{"The records are incomplete"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"intl"} /><span>{"A guideline from another country is being relied on"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"p35"} checked={true} /><span>{"The report is going to court"}</span></label> </div> </div> <div className={"tout"} data-out={""}><div className={"tout__hd"}><b>{"The framework for this case"}</b><span>{"England and Wales"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--hd trow--txt"}><b>{"Element"}</b><span>{"What the law and the rules actually require"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"The standard of care in England and Wales"}</b><span><b>{"Breach of duty is measured against the standard of the ordinary skilled practitioner professing to have that special skill"}</b>{" — the "}<i>{"Bolam"}</i>{" test, from "}<i>{"Bolam v Friern Hospital Management Committee"}</i>{" [1957]. A doctor is not negligent if they acted in accordance with a practice accepted as proper by a responsible body of medical opinion skilled in that particular art. "}<b><i>{"Bolitho v City and Hackney Health Authority"}</i>{" [1998] added the qualification that matters:"}</b>{" the court must be satisfied that the body of opinion relied on has a "}<i>{"logical basis"}</i>{", and that its proponents have directed their minds to the comparative risks and benefits and reached a defensible conclusion. A practice is not reasonable merely because some practitioners follow it. An expert report that recites Bolam without engaging with Bolitho is doing half the job, and the opposing expert will say so."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--has"}><b>{"Duty, breach, causation, damage"}</b><span>{"The four elements, in the order they have to be established, and the order a well-built report follows. "}<b>{"Duty"}</b>{" is usually admitted in a treatment case and is occasionally the whole argument where a duty is asserted outside a treating relationship. "}<b>{"Breach"}</b>{" is the standard-of-care question above. "}<b>{"Causation"}</b>{" is where most claims are actually won and lost — and it is where reports most often stop short. "}<b>{"Damage"}</b>{" must be a recognised injury, and proving breach without proving that the breach caused the damage complained of establishes nothing. A report that demonstrates substandard care and does not address causation has not helped the instructing solicitor."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"Citing levels of evidence and grades of recommendation"}</b><span><b>{"Name the framework, every time."}</b>{" Letters and numbers mean different things in different systems, and “Level A evidence” unqualified is ambiguous rather than simply wrong — which in a report that will be cross-examined is the same problem. In the "}<b>{"ACC/AHA"}</b>{" system, "}<i>{"Level of Evidence"}</i>{" A, B-R, B-NR, C-LD and C-EO describes the evidence, while "}<i>{"Class of Recommendation"}</i>{" 1, 2a, 2b and 3 describes the strength of the recommendation — so Level A is genuinely a level of evidence there. In "}<b>{"GRADE"}</b>{", certainty is high, moderate, low or very low and recommendations are strong or conditional; there is no Level A. The "}<b>{"Oxford Centre for Evidence-Based Medicine"}</b>{" uses numbered levels, 1 to 5, in its 2011 table. "}<b>{"SIGN"}</b>{" uses numbered levels of evidence and lettered grades of recommendation, so a SIGN “Grade A” and an ACC/AHA “Level A” are different constructs sharing a letter. A phrase such as “integration of Level A evidence” with no framework named beside it does not say which of these is meant, and the difference changes the claim."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"The report is going to court in England and Wales"}</b><span><b>{"Then CPR Part 35 and Practice Direction 35 govern it, and the duties are not negotiable."}</b>{" Rule 35.3: “It is the duty of experts to help the court on matters within their expertise”, and “this duty overrides any obligation to the person from whom experts have received instructions or by whom they are paid.” PD 35 requires that expert evidence be “the independent product of the expert uninfluenced by the pressures of litigation”; that the expert not assume the role of advocate; that they consider all material facts "}<i>{"including those which might detract from their opinion"}</i>{"; that they make clear when a question falls outside their expertise and when they cannot reach a definite opinion; and that any material change of view be communicated without delay. Rule 35.10 requires the report to state the substance of all material instructions, written or oral, on which it was written — and that material is not protected from disclosure in the ordinary way. The report ends with the statement of truth at PD 35 paragraph 3.3, beginning “I confirm that I have made clear which facts and matters referred to in this report are within my own knowledge and which are not.” "}<b>{"Consider all material facts"}</b>{" is the provision most often breached in practice, and it is breached by omission rather than by anything deliberate."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--has"}><b>{"Instructed by the claimant"}</b><span>{"The same discipline applies whichever side instructs: the material facts that cut against the case go in the report. An expert who omits them has breached the duty that overrides the instruction, and the omission is found in cross-examination rather than in the office."}</span></div><div className={"tverd"}><p><b>{"Pre-action."}</b>{" The chronology is the work. A timed, sourced chronology with every entry referenced to a page in the bundle is what every later document is built from, and it is the artefact that survives a change of expert or counsel. "}<b>{"And what we are:"}</b>{" we are a medical record review, chronology, literature and drafting service. We are not solicitors and this is not legal advice. We do not decide whether a claim should be brought, settled or defended — that is for the instructing lawyer — and we do not offer a view on quantum. Where an opinion on the medicine is required, it is given by a clinician practising in the relevant specialty, who signs it in their own name and owes the duty to the court that overrides every other obligation, including to whoever is paying. A supplier who offers a “strong case” is offering you something an expert cannot properly provide; what an expert provides is a "}<i>{"defensible"}</i>{" one, and the difference is the whole of the professional obligation."}</p></div><p className={"tmeth"}><b>{"Sources, and three corrections."}</b>{" CPR Part 35 and Practice Direction 35 read at justice.gov.uk on 22 September 2026, including rule 35.3 on the overriding duty, rule 35.10 on material instructions, and the statement of truth at PD 35 paragraph 3.3. The National Medical Commission’s own site, nmc.org.in, read the same day, confirming its establishment under the National Medical Commission Act 2019 and describing the MCI as erstwhile. The Oxford Centre for Evidence-Based Medicine levels of evidence at cebm.ox.ac.uk. Case citations as reported. "}<b>{"What is worth checking on any medico-legal page."}</b>{" “Standard of care analysis aligned with international guidelines” — there is no international standard of care, it is set by the jurisdiction. The "}<b>{"MCI"}</b>{" listed among Indian regulators, or hedged as “MCI/NMC”, when it no longer exists. “Level A evidence” with no framework named beside it. And section 43A of the Information Technology Act 2000 given as the Indian data-protection basis, when India has enacted the "}<b>{"Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023"}</b>{"; we confirm its commencement and rules position at the start of any Indian instruction rather than asserting a status we have not checked. "}<b>{"This tool is a planning aid, not legal advice"}</b>{", and nothing in it substitutes for the instructing lawyer’s judgement on the law of their own jurisdiction."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> </div></section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-our-experts-10dcxgw"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Scope, judgement, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, the reporting guideline"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"The applicable checklist"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, ICH E9"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on, and records it so somebody else could find it again. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-sample-work-owb8os"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The chronology, which is what everything else is built from."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"An opinion is only as good as the record analysis under it. This is a real records review and chronology from a clinical negligence instruction, with every identifying detail changed — including the part clients least expect, where the review concluded against the case it was instructed to support. Use the tabs, then open the full pack."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Records review and chronology"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"Clinical negligence · 1,140 pages · claimant instruction"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"Records · chronology · breach · causation"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the review"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"ml-t1"} aria-controls={"ml-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"Records"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"ml-t2"} aria-controls={"ml-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Chronology"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"ml-t3"} aria-controls={"ml-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"Breach"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"ml-t4"} aria-controls={"ml-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Causation"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"ml-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"ml-t1"}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The observation chart for the critical 14 hours was not in the bundle"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Requested, not supplied, and not noticed until the records were reconciled against the request. It is the single most important document in a deterioration case and the claim could not be properly assessed without it. Chased at day two rather than at the report stage, which saved roughly a month."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Out-of-hours and ambulance records missing entirely"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Held by two different organisations, neither included in the original request. Both materially relevant to the timeline. Listed, requested, and the chronology marked to show what could not yet be established."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Two pagination sequences in one bundle"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The hospital records and the GP records were separately numbered, with overlapping page numbers. Every reference in an earlier letter was therefore ambiguous. Repaginated once, and all subsequent documents reference the single sequence."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Imaging reports present; images themselves not"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"A distinction that matters. The report is one radiologist’s contemporaneous reading; the images allow another to disagree with it. Where the reading is in issue, the images have to be obtained, and in this case they were."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"1,140 pages received"}</span><span>{"4 categories of record missing"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"ml-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"ml-t2"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Entries"}</dt><dd>{"612 in the chronology, each with its source and page reference in the repaginated bundle."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Timed rather than dated"}</dt><dd>{"Wherever the record gives a time. In a deterioration case the interval between an observation and a response is the case, and a chronology to the day cannot support a counterfactual."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Conflicts between records"}</dt><dd>{"7. The most significant: the nursing note and the medical note give different times for the same review, forty minutes apart. Both recorded, neither reconciled by us — which of the two is right is a matter for evidence, not for a records reviewer."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Entries that could not be read"}</dt><dd>{"11 handwritten entries, 4 of them in the relevant window. Marked as illegible rather than interpreted. A guess in a chronology becomes a fact in a report and then a problem in a witness box."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Gaps marked"}</dt><dd>{"The fourteen hours covered by the missing observation chart, shown as a gap rather than bridged. A chronology that reads continuously over an absent record is the document that discredits the report built on it."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Retrospective entries identified"}</dt><dd>{"3, made after the event and timed to the event. Flagged with the time of writing where the system recorded it. Not an allegation — an observation the instructing solicitor needs to have."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"ml-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"ml-t3"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The guidance in force at the material time was identified and dated"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Not the current version. The relevant national guidance had been revised in the interval, and the revision changed the threshold at issue. Analysing 2021 care against 2026 guidance is hindsight dressed as standard, and the defence would have said so."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The local protocol differed from national guidance"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"And the local protocol was the one in operation. Both obtained and both set out. Under Bolitho a practice is not reasonable merely because it is local, but the fact that it was the protocol is material and the report has to engage with it rather than ignore it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"A foreign guideline had been cited in the letter of claim"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"It said what the claimant wanted and it does not set the standard in this jurisdiction. Retained as supporting material, clearly labelled, with the governing domestic standard doing the work. Left as the primary authority it would have weakened the case, not strengthened it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The material facts cutting against the claim were listed"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Four of them, including one that substantially explains the delay. PD 35 requires an expert to consider all material facts including those detracting from their opinion, and a claimant solicitor needs them before the letter of response arrives rather than after."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Contemporaneous standard established"}</span><span>{"4 facts against the claim, listed"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"ml-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"ml-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The counterfactual"}</dt><dd>{"Written out: had the escalation occurred at the point the claimant says it should have, what would have happened and when. Stated as a sequence with times, not as an assertion that the outcome would have been different."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The causal standard"}</dt><dd>{"Named. "}<i>{"But for"}</i>{" was the standard applied, and the analysis says so — an unlabelled causation opinion is the one that collapses when counsel asks which test is being used."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Where the analysis stopped"}</dt><dd>{"At the point the records could not carry it. The fourteen-hour gap prevents a firm view on when deterioration became detectable, and the review says so rather than estimating."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The conclusion"}</dt><dd><b>{"The breach argument is arguable; the causation argument, on these records, is not yet."}</b>{" That was not the conclusion the instruction was hoping for and it was the honest one on the material available."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What would change it"}</dt><dd>{"Three specific documents, named. Two arrived six weeks later; one did not exist. With them the causation analysis became sustainable, which is why the review said what it needed rather than declining to conclude."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What we did not do"}</dt><dd>{"We did not advise on limitation, on quantum, on whether to proceed, or on settlement. Those are the instructing solicitor’s, and the review says so in writing."}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · specialty, facts, parties and every figure changed"}</span><span>{"Records review, as delivered"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"One bundle, 1,140 pages, read against the four elements. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each part."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The records tab is the finding that saved a month."}</b>{" The observation chart for the critical fourteen hours was requested and never supplied, and nobody had noticed because nobody had reconciled what arrived against what was asked for. Found at day two it is a chasing letter. Found at the report stage it is a month, and possibly a report that has to be withdrawn."}</p> <p><b>{"The causation tab is the one worth reading closely."}</b>{" The review concluded that causation was not made out on the records available — against the interest of the party instructing it. Then it named the three documents that would change that, two of which arrived. A review that tells an instructing solicitor only what they want is a review they cannot rely on."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Records reconciled against the request"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Before anything is read for content."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Timed entries, page-referenced"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Because causation turns on intervals."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"The standard as it was at the time"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Not the current version of the guidance."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"The facts against the case, listed"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Whichever side instructs."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a review built round a matter like yours — same jurisdiction, same specialty, same stage."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-ml"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-ml"}>{"Read the full review"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-ml"}> <span><b>{"Read the full review"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the records reconciliation, the chronology method, the breach analysis, the causation analysis and what is handed over"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-ml"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Medico-legal support · sample records review"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Records review and chronology — clinical negligence, claimant instruction"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"A real review with the specialty, the facts, the parties, the dates and every figure changed. The method, the categories of finding and the reporting format are as delivered. Ask us and we will build one around a matter like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"Records reconciliation, before anything is read"}</h4> <p>{"The first pass is administrative and it is the one that saves the most time. What was requested, what arrived, what is absent, and what the absence prevents."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Finding"}</th><th>{"What was done"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td><b>{"Observation chart missing for 14 hours"}</b></td><td>{"Requested and not supplied. In a deterioration case it is the single most important document, and the claim cannot be properly assessed without it. Identified on day two and chased immediately, which saved roughly a month against finding it at the report stage."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"Out-of-hours and ambulance records absent"}</b></td><td>{"Held by two organisations neither of which was in the original request. Both materially relevant to the timeline. Listed and requested, with the chronology marked to show what could not yet be established."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"Two pagination sequences"}</b></td><td>{"Hospital and GP records separately numbered with overlapping page numbers, making every reference in earlier correspondence ambiguous. Repaginated once; every subsequent document references the single sequence."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"Imaging reports without images"}</b></td><td>{"A distinction that matters: the report is one radiologist’s contemporaneous reading, the images let another disagree with it. Where the reading is in issue, the images are needed. They were obtained."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"Duplicate sets"}</b></td><td>{"Roughly 180 pages duplicated across two disclosures. Deduplicated with the duplicates listed rather than discarded, so nobody later believes something is missing."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"The missing-records list goes to the instructing solicitor on the day it is produced, not with the finished review. Chasing a nursing chart takes weeks; discovering you need it at the end of the process costs a month and sometimes a limitation problem."}</p> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"The chronology, and the rules it follows"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Element"}</th><th>{"Method"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Entries"}</td><td>{"612, each with its source document and page reference in the repaginated bundle."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Times, not dates"}</td><td>{"Recorded wherever the record gives one. In a deterioration case the interval between an observation and a response "}<i>{"is"}</i>{" the case, and a chronology to the day cannot support a counterfactual."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Conflicts"}</td><td>{"7 recorded. The most significant: nursing and medical notes give times forty minutes apart for the same review. Both recorded; neither reconciled by us. Which is correct is a matter for evidence, not for a records reviewer, and a review that quietly picks one has made a finding it has no basis to make."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Illegible entries"}</td><td>{"11, four of them in the relevant window. Marked illegible rather than interpreted. A guess in a chronology becomes a fact in a report and then a problem in a witness box."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Gaps"}</td><td>{"Shown as gaps. The fourteen hours covered by the missing observation chart is not bridged, inferred or smoothed. A chronology that reads continuously over an absent record is the document that discredits the report built on it."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Retrospective entries"}</td><td>{"3 identified, made after the event and timed to it, flagged with the time of writing where the system recorded it. Not an allegation — an observation the instructing solicitor needs to hold."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Abbreviations and drug names"}</td><td>{"Expanded on first use, with local abbreviations checked against the trust’s own list rather than assumed."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"Breach of duty, against the standard as it was"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Question"}</th><th>{"What was established"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Which standard governs"}</td><td>{"England and Wales: "}<i>{"Bolam"}</i>{", as qualified by "}<i>{"Bolitho"}</i>{". The analysis engages with the Bolitho qualification rather than reciting Bolam — whether the body of opinion relied on has a logical basis, and whether its proponents weighed the comparative risks and benefits."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Which guidance was in force"}</td><td>{"The version current at the material time, identified and dated. The relevant national guidance had been revised since, and the revision changed the threshold at issue. Measuring care against a guideline published afterwards is hindsight dressed as a standard, and the defence would have said so in one line."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The local protocol"}</td><td>{"Differed from national guidance, and was the protocol in operation. Both obtained, both set out. Under Bolitho a practice is not reasonable merely because it is local, but the fact that it was the protocol is material and the analysis has to engage with it."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The foreign guideline in the letter of claim"}</td><td>{"Cited as though it set the standard. It does not. Retained as supporting material and clearly labelled as such, with the governing domestic standard doing the work. "}<b>{"Left as the primary authority it would have weakened the claim"}</b>{", and it is exactly the error behind an offer of analysis “aligned with international guidelines”."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Facts cutting against the claim"}</td><td>{"Four, listed. One substantially explains the delay complained of. PD 35 requires an expert to consider all material facts including those detracting from their opinion; separately, a claimant solicitor needs them before the letter of response arrives rather than after."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Evidence levels cited"}</td><td>{"Framework named every time. An unqualified “Level A” means different things in ACC/AHA, GRADE, SIGN and the Oxford CEBM tables, and ambiguity in a document that will be cross-examined is a defect whether or not it is an error."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"Causation, and where the analysis stopped"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Element"}</th><th>{"What the review said"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"The counterfactual"}</td><td>{"Written out as a sequence with times: had escalation occurred at the point contended for, what would have happened and when. Not asserted as “the outcome would have been different”, which is a conclusion rather than an analysis."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The causal standard applied"}</td><td><i>{"But for"}</i>{", named explicitly. Where the facts had supported it, material contribution or loss of a chance would have been named instead. An unlabelled causation opinion is the one that collapses when counsel asks which test is being applied."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Where the records ran out"}</td><td>{"The fourteen-hour gap prevents a firm view on when deterioration became detectable. The review says so rather than estimating across it."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"The conclusion"}</b></td><td><b>{"Breach: arguable. Causation, on the records then available: not made out."}</b>{" That was not what the instruction was hoping for. It was the honest answer on the material in the bundle, and it was given at screening stage rather than after a full report."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"What would change it"}</td><td>{"Three documents, named specifically. Two arrived six weeks later; the third did not exist. With them the causation analysis became sustainable — which is why the review identified what it needed rather than simply declining to conclude."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"What we did not do"}</td><td>{"No advice on limitation, quantum, prospects of success or settlement. Those belong to the instructing solicitor, and the review says so in writing so the boundary is on the record."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"Who signs what"}</h4> <p>{"This matters more in this field than in any other we work in, so it is set out rather than assumed."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Document"}</th><th>{"Who produces it, and who owes what"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Records reconciliation, chronology, missing-records list"}</td><td>{"Us. Factual work product for the instructing lawyer. No opinion on the medicine."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Literature and guideline research"}</td><td>{"Us. Documented and re-runnable, with the version in force at the material time identified."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The clinical opinion"}</td><td><b>{"A clinician practising in the relevant specialty, who signs it in their own name."}</b>{" Under CPR Part 35 their duty is to help the court on matters within their expertise, and that duty overrides any obligation to whoever instructed or paid them. We prepare the material the opinion rests on and draft to their instruction; we do not write their opinion for them."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The CPR Part 35 report"}</td><td>{"Signed by the expert, containing the statement of truth at PD 35 paragraph 3.3, and stating the substance of all material instructions under rule 35.10 — material that is not protected from disclosure in the ordinary way."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Legal advice"}</td><td>{"Not us. Limitation, prospects, strategy, quantum and settlement belong to the instructing lawyer, and a supplier drifting into them is creating a problem for the client rather than solving one."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"6"}</span>{"What was handed over"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Artefact"}</th><th>{"Why it matters afterwards"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"The repaginated, indexed bundle"}</td><td>{"One sequence, so every later reference is unambiguous."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The chronology"}</td><td>{"612 entries, timed and page-referenced, with conflicts, illegible entries and gaps marked. It survives a change of expert, of counsel or of firm, and it is what a joint statement is built from months later."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The missing-records schedule"}</td><td>{"What was requested, received, absent, chased and outstanding, with what each absence prevents."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The contemporaneous guidance pack"}</td><td>{"The version in force at the material time, dated, with the local protocol alongside it."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The search log"}</td><td>{"Every literature search with its database, interface, date and result count, so it can be re-run rather than repeated."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The adverse-facts schedule"}</td><td>{"Material that cuts against the instructing party. Uncomfortable, required, and better in your hands than in the other side’s alone."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"A note on the boundary"}</td><td>{"What we did, what we did not do, and what remains with the instructing lawyer. The shortest document in the pack and the one that prevents the next misunderstanding."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}><b>{"What we do not claim:"}</b>{" that a case is strong. “Defensible” is the right word, and it is the only one of the two we will use. “Strong” is a judgement for the instructing lawyer, made on material the record-reviewer does not hold. What a review of this kind reliably changes is that the records are complete or known to be incomplete, that the chronology can carry a counterfactual, that the standard applied is the one that governs, and that the facts against the case are in your hands before they are in the other side’s. Those are worth buying on their own terms, and they are worth more when the answer goes against the instruction."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Benefits of reconciling the records first"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What it changes, and what it cannot."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"No supplier makes a case stronger. What a properly built record analysis changes is whether the case is judged on what the records show, and whether you find the weaknesses before the other side does."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Missing records surface on day two"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Reconciling what arrived against what was requested takes an afternoon. Discovering at the report stage that the observation chart was never supplied costs a month, and sometimes a limitation problem."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The chronology can carry a counterfactual"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Timed entries, page-referenced, with gaps and conflicts marked. A chronology to the day cannot support a causation argument, and causation is where most claims are decided."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The standard is the one that applied then"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The guidance in force at the material time, identified and dated, with the local protocol alongside. Measuring past care against current guidance is hindsight, and the other side will say so in one line."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"You hold the adverse facts first"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The material that cuts against your client, scheduled, whichever side instructs. Required by the rules, and better in your hands before the letter of response than in theirs alone."}</span></span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-packages-1dyagzp"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Four tiers, with prices and page caps."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Record review is commonly packaged with real inclusions and "}<b>{"not one price or turnaround between them"}</b>{" — turnaround given only as prose, with basic consultations that “may take a few hours” and comprehensive reports that “could take several days”. For a service sold to solicitors and insurers working to court deadlines, that is not a specification. Here are the figures, with the page caps printed beside them, because in record review the page count is the work."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers tiers--4 rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Screen"}</span> <h3>{"Is there a case in these records?"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"A first look before committing to a full review — and the answer is often no, which is the point"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $650"}</b><span>{"up to 300 pages · triage only · no formal report"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"5 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Whether there is an arguable breach on the face of the records"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Whether there is an arguable causal link to the damage claimed"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"What is missing from the bundle, listed and specified"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Anything in the records that kills it, said plainly"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A recommendation on whether a full review is worth the cost"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Credited in full against a full review commissioned within 60 days."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-ml"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-ml"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Screen"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Review"}</span> <h3>{"Records review and clinical chronology"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"The document everything else is built from, and the one that survives a change of expert or counsel"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $1,600"}</b><span>{"up to 1,000 pages · $1.60/page above · 2 revision rounds"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"10 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Screen, then the full analysis"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Records reconciled against the request; bundle repaginated and indexed"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Timed, page-referenced chronology with conflicts and gaps marked"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Illegible entries flagged rather than interpreted"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Retrospective entries identified where the system records them"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A missing-records schedule, delivered on the day it is produced"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Most instructions start here. The chronology is reusable through the life of the matter."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-ml"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-ml"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Review"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Analysis"}</span> <h3>{"Breach and causation, with the literature"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Where the case is going forward and the argument has to be built against the governing standard"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $3,400"}</b><span>{"up to 1,000 pages · search log included · 3 rounds"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"15 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Review, at analysis depth"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The guidance in force at the material time, identified and dated"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Local protocol obtained and set out alongside national guidance"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Breach analysed against the governing standard, Bolitho engaged not recited"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Causation with the counterfactual written out and the test named"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A schedule of material facts cutting against the instructing party"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Consent cases are analysed under Montgomery, not Bolam. It is not an upgrade; it is the law."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-ml"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-ml"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Analysis"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Report"}</span> <h3>{"Drafting support for a report to the court"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Where a CPR Part 35 report, a state-court report or an affidavit of merit is required"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $6,500"}</b><span>{"including clinician opinion · unlimited rounds in scope"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"20 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Analysis, drafted to the rules of the court"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Opinion by a clinician practising in the relevant specialty, signed in their name"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The form, contents and statement of truth the rules require"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Every proposition traced to the page that supports it"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Support for the joint statement and the expert discussion afterwards"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"The expert’s duty is to the court and overrides the instruction. That is not negotiable and it is the point."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-ml"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-ml"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Report"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"psv rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The chronology"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"Every entry"}</b><span>{"timed and page-referenced"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"With conflicts, gaps and illegible entries marked"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Timed rather than dated, because causation turns on intervals. Conflicts between records recorded rather than reconciled, because which is right is a matter for evidence. It survives a change of expert, counsel or firm, and it is what a joint statement is built from a year later."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The missing-records schedule"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"On day two"}</b><span>{"not with the report"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Requested, received, absent, chased"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"And what each absence prevents you from concluding. Chasing a nursing chart takes weeks; finding out you needed it at the end of the process costs a month. This is the cheapest document we produce and the one that most often changes a timetable."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The adverse-facts schedule"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"Whichever side"}</b><span>{"instructs us"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"The material that cuts against your client"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Required of an expert by PD 35, which says all material facts must be considered including those which might detract from the opinion. Also simply useful: you want these before the letter of response, not after. It is the document clients least enjoy and most rely on."}</p> </div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Priced alongside any tier: literature and guideline research as a standalone piece, with a re-runnable search log; review of another expert’s report, identifying where the disagreement actually is; preparation for a joint statement or expert discussion; chronologies for inquests and internal investigations, which take a different format and tone; medical summaries for insurers at volume, to a consistent schema; translation of records with clinical terminology checked rather than rendered literally; and expedited delivery where capacity allows, quoted on capacity rather than urgency."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#/pricing"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-guarantee-nyg1yo"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"In this field the limits are the product. A supplier who will tell you what the records do not support is worth more than one who will tell you what you hoped."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Revision until the analysis meets the instruction and the rules of the court it is going to, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed, and the reviewer available when the joint statement or the conference comes round rather than reassigned."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Every line traced to a page"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Each entry in the chronology and each proposition in the analysis referenced to the document that supports it, in one pagination sequence."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Gaps stay gaps"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"We do not bridge a missing record, interpret an illegible entry or reconcile a conflict between two notes. Each is marked as what it is, because a guess becomes a fact and then a problem in a witness box."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"The adverse facts are scheduled"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Whichever side instructs. The rules require it of an expert, and you need them before the other side has them."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A page mis-referenced, a guideline version wrong, a record missed in the bundle — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b> <b>{"We are not solicitors and nothing we produce is legal advice"}</b>{" — not on limitation, prospects, quantum, strategy or settlement, all of which belong to the instructing lawyer. "}<b>{"We are not the expert witness."}</b>{" Where an opinion on the medicine is required it is given by a clinician practising in the relevant specialty, who signs it in their own name and whose duty to the court, under CPR Part 35, overrides any obligation to whoever instructed or paid them. We prepare the material the opinion rests on. "}<b>{"We do not promise a strong case"}</b>{", and we will not use that phrasing: defensible is the word, and strength is a judgement for the instructing lawyer on material a record-reviewer does not hold. We will not omit material that cuts against the instructing party, we will not interpret an illegible entry or bridge a missing record to make a chronology read continuously, and we will not give an opinion outside the specialty of the clinician giving it. We do not accept instructions on both sides of the same matter, and where a conflict exists we say so before accepting rather than managing it quietly. We do not provide analysis “aligned with international guidelines” — the standard of care is set by the jurisdiction, and foreign guidance is supporting material, labelled as such. And where the answer is that the case is not made out on these records, that is what the review will say."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"The missing-records check is free"}</p> <p>{"Send the index of what you received and the request that produced it, and we will tell you within two business days what is absent, what is likely to be held by a different organisation, and what each absence prevents you from establishing. No cost, no obligation. It takes us an hour or two and it is the single most time-critical thing in a records case — an observation chart chased at week one is a letter; chased at month four it is a month, and occasionally a limitation problem."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Patient data handled as what it is"}</p> <p>{"Special category health data, under a non-disclosure agreement signed before any material moves, held under the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018 on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015 — certificate H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N. Access limited to the named reviewers on the matter, retention to the period the instruction requires, secure deletion on your instruction, and never used to train anything. Where an instruction touches another jurisdiction’s regime — HIPAA in the United States, India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 — we confirm the current position at the start of that instruction rather than relying on what was true last time."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Conflicts declared before acceptance"}</p> <p>{"We do not act on both sides of the same matter, and we check before accepting rather than discovering later. Where a clinician we would ordinarily instruct has a connection to a party, an institution or a previous instruction in the same matter, you are told and we propose somebody else. In a field where an expert’s independence is the first thing tested in cross-examination, a conflict managed quietly is a conflict that becomes the story."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Working to your precedents, not ours"}</p> <p>{"Your chronology format, your bundle conventions, your pagination, your report precedents and your case management system. Firms and insurers that handle volume have formats their own people can read at speed, and a supplier introducing a different one is creating work rather than saving it. Where you have no format we will propose one and document it. And where a matter runs for years, the same reviewer stays with it, because the value of a chronology is partly in the person who remembers why a line is marked."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-client-stories-1c4k2y1"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three instructions, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named client has confirmed it in writing. Nothing here claims a case outcome, because no record reviewer produces one."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They found the observation chart had never been supplied. We had been working on the bundle for six weeks without noticing.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"CLINICAL"}<br />{"NEGLIGENCE"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Records"}<br />{"Review"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Partner · firm to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Chronology and missing-records schedule"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“The analysis said causation was not made out on the records we had. We did not enjoy reading it and it was right.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"CAUSATION"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Breach and"}<br />{"Causation"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Solicitor · firm to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Analysis and adverse-facts schedule"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“The guidance our letter of claim relied on had been revised after the treatment. They dated it before we sent anything.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"STANDARD"}<br />{"OF CARE"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Guideline"}<br />{"Research"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Claims manager · organisation to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Contemporaneous guidance pack and search log"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""}><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot is-on"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 1"} /><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 2"} /></div> <div className={"tcar__btns"}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-medico-legal-faq-10jolmm"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Medico-legal support FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Nine questions instructing parties ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure whether there is a case in the records? Send them and we will tell you in five business days. "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-0"}><span>{"Are you the expert witness, or the people who help the expert?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-0"} role={"region"}><div><p><b>{"The second, and the distinction is the most important thing on this page."}</b>{" We are a medical record review, chronology, literature and drafting service. Where an opinion on the medicine is required, it is given by a clinician practising in the relevant specialty who signs it in their own name — and whose duty, under CPR Part 35, is to help the court on matters within their expertise, a duty that “overrides any obligation to the person from whom experts have received instructions or by whom they are paid”. We prepare the material that opinion rests on: the reconciled bundle, the timed chronology, the contemporaneous guidance, the literature with its search log, and the adverse-facts schedule. We do not write an expert’s opinion for them, and a supplier who offers to is offering something that will not survive cross-examination about how the report came to be written."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-1"}><span>{"What is the standard of care, and is it international?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-1"} role={"region"}><div><p><b>{"No, and it is worth saying why not."}</b>{" “Standard of care analysis aligned with international guidelines” is offered widely in this market, and there is no international standard of care. It is set by the law of the jurisdiction and, in practice, by what a responsible body of practitioners there would have done at the time — and it is usually the contested issue in the claim. In England and Wales that is "}<i>{"Bolam"}</i>{", as qualified by "}<i>{"Bolitho"}</i>{": a practice accepted as proper by a responsible body of medical opinion, provided that body’s view has a logical basis and its proponents weighed the comparative risks and benefits. In the United States it is set state by state, with most states applying a national professional standard for specialists. In India the line runs through "}<i>{"Jacob Mathew"}</i>{". A guideline from another country can be persuasive supporting evidence and it does not set the standard — and a report that leans on it in place of the governing standard is weaker, not stronger. Opposing counsel will make that point and they will be right."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-2"}><span>{"Which Indian regulator governs this work?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Not the one still named on a great many pages, and on material sold for legal and regulatory accuracy that matters. "}<b>{"The Medical Council of India no longer exists."}</b>{" It was replaced by the "}<b>{"National Medical Commission"}</b>{", established under the National Medical Commission Act 2019 — the NMC’s own website refers throughout to the “erstwhile MCI”. Pages naming the MCI among the regulators they work to, or hedging with “MCI/NMC”, are citing a body that no longer exists — and hedging is worse than choosing either. Two related points: section 43A of the Information Technology Act 2000 is no longer the live Indian data-protection basis, because India has enacted the "}<b>{"Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023"}</b>{" — we were not able to confirm that Act’s current commencement and rules position, so rather than assert a status we have not checked, we confirm it at the start of any Indian instruction. And “Level A evidence” cited with no framework named is ambiguous rather than wrong — but ambiguity in a document that gets cross-examined is a defect either way."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-3"}><span>{"Does Bolam apply to consent?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, and this is the most common error we find in older medico-legal reports. "}<i>{"Montgomery v Lanarkshire Health Board"}</i>{" [2015] UKSC 11 — a Scottish appeal binding across the UK — replaced the professional-practice test for information disclosure with a patient-centred one. The doctor must take reasonable care to ensure the patient is aware of any "}<b>{"material risk"}</b>{" in the recommended treatment and of any reasonable alternatives, with materiality judged by what a reasonable person in the patient’s position would attach significance to, or what the doctor is or should reasonably be aware this particular patient would attach significance to. So a consent analysis measured against what a responsible body of doctors would have disclosed is applying a test that has not been the law for over a decade — and the defence will identify it in a paragraph. Where consent is in issue the analysis is built on Montgomery and the records are read for what the patient was actually told, by whom and when, which is frequently the part of the record that is thinnest."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-4"}><span>{"What must a report going to court contain?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"In England and Wales, CPR Part 35 and Practice Direction 35 govern. Rule 35.3 sets the overriding duty to help the court, which displaces any obligation to whoever instructed or paid. PD 35 requires the evidence to be “the independent product of the expert uninfluenced by the pressures of litigation”; that the expert not assume the role of advocate; that they "}<b>{"consider all material facts, including those which might detract from their opinion"}</b>{"; that they make clear when a question falls outside their expertise and when they cannot reach a definite view; and that any material change of opinion be communicated without delay. Rule 35.10 requires the report to state the substance of all material instructions, written or oral, and that material is not protected from disclosure in the ordinary way. The report ends with the statement of truth at PD 35 paragraph 3.3. "}<b>{"The “all material facts” requirement is the one most often breached"}</b>{", and it is breached by omission rather than by anything deliberate — which is why the adverse-facts schedule is part of what we deliver. Other courts have other rules, and a report drafted to the wrong rulebook is challenged on its form before anyone argues about its substance."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-5"}><span>{"What is different about a United States instruction?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"The state is the first question, not a detail. The standard of care is set state by state; most states apply a national professional standard for specialists while some retain or modify a locality rule. Many states require an "}<b>{"affidavit or certificate of merit"}</b>{" from a qualified expert before a malpractice claim may proceed at all, with the qualifying criteria and the deadline set by statute — a claim can be dismissed on that alone, before anyone reaches the medicine. Admissibility in federal court is governed by "}<b>{"Federal Rule of Evidence 702"}</b>{", amended with effect from "}<b>{"1 December 2023"}</b>{" to make explicit that the proponent must show admissibility is more likely than not, and that the opinion reflects a reliable application of the methodology to the facts — addressing courts that had been treating overstatement as going to weight rather than admissibility. Some states apply the older "}<i>{"Frye"}</i>{" general-acceptance test instead. We draft to the rules of the court the report is going to, and we ask which court before we start."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-6"}><span>{"How quickly can we get a review?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"A screening review of up to 300 pages in "}<b>{"5 business days"}</b>{"; a full records review and chronology to 1,000 pages in "}<b>{"10"}</b>{"; breach and causation analysis in "}<b>{"15"}</b>{"; drafting support for a report to the court in "}<b>{"20"}</b>{". Turnaround in this market is usually given as prose — basic consultations “may take a few hours”, comprehensive reports “could take several days” — which is not something a buyer working to a court deadline can plan around. Two things move a real timeline more than page count. "}<b>{"Missing records"}</b>{", which is why the reconciliation happens first and the schedule reaches you on the day it is produced. And "}<b>{"a clinician’s calendar"}</b>{" where an opinion is needed, which is a person rather than a process step. Expedited work is available where capacity allows and is quoted on capacity rather than on urgency; where a date is not achievable we say so rather than taking the instruction and missing it."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-7"}><span>{"How is patient data handled?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"As special category health data, which is what it is. A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves. Records are held under the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018 on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015 — certificate H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N — with access limited to the named reviewers on the matter, retention for the period the instruction requires, secure deletion on your instruction, and no use in training anything. Where an instruction touches another regime — HIPAA in the United States, India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 — we confirm the current position at the start of that instruction rather than relying on what was true at the last one. We will also work entirely inside your own document management system where you require it; several of our clients do, and it is a reasonable thing to require."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"ml-8"}><span>{"Will you tell us if the case is weak?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"ml-8"} role={"region"}><div><p><b>{"Yes, and that is most of what you are buying."}</b>{" The sample review on this page concluded that causation was not made out on the records then available — against the interest of the party who instructed it — and then named the three documents that would change that, two of which arrived. A review that tells an instructing solicitor only what they hoped is a review they cannot rely on, and an expert who cannot concede anything is not believed on the points where they are right. Two related commitments. We schedule the material facts that cut against the instructing party, whichever side instructs, because PD 35 requires an expert to consider all material facts including those detracting from their opinion, and because you want them before the other side has them. And we do not promise a “strong case”, however often it is offered elsewhere: strength is a judgement for the instructing lawyer, made on material a record reviewer does not hold. "}<b>{"Defensible"}</b>{" is the word, and it was already the right one elsewhere on the same page."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of a medico-legal instruction."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"The evidence the standard is established from, and the clinical writing that uses the same record-reading discipline."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"ESTABLISHING THE STANDARD"}</b><em>{"evidence and guidance"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/literature-search-and-citation/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Literature search and citation"}</b><span>{"Re-runnable searches, with the version in force at the material time."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/clinical-literature-review-for-an-evidence-based-medicine/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Clinical literature review"}</b><span>{"Evidence appraised and graded with the framework named."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"THE SAME RECORDS, OTHER USES"}</b><em>{"clinical writing"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Case report writing"}</b><span>{"Where a case becomes a publication rather than a claim, under CARE."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Physician writing services"}</b><span>{"The wider set of writing built on reading a clinical record properly."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"REGULATED DOCUMENTS"}</b><em>{"where the rules are written down"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/medical-writing/regulatory-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Regulatory writing"}</b><span>{"Documents written to a named governing instrument, checked for version."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/medical-writing/editorial-quality-support-service/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Editorial and quality support"}</b><span>{"Independent checking of documents written elsewhere."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces on structure, journal choice and clarity in clinical writing."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"A set structure, clear objectives, and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"A strategic read of which journals still publish them, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Clear materials change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send the index. The missing-records check is free."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Two business days, at no cost: what is absent from the bundle, what is likely held by a different organisation, and what each absence prevents you from establishing. It takes us an hour or two and it is the most time-critical thing in a records case."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
